## Materials:
Rod: Attached to fsr for S-hook to hang from
Bucket: for water collection
S-hook: to connect bucket handle to rod; normalizes force
Peristaltic pump / water dispenser / garden hose: to provide steady flow of water into bucket
Clamp: holds rod to surface(table) to prevent any movement as force increases
Tape: for the fsr to stay stuck to rod
FSR system

## Continuous 
Steps:
Stabilize FSR on table, attached to glove and facing upwards. 
Place T130X calculator in glove underneath FSR
Attach the bucket to one end of the S-hook, and hook the other end onto the rod over the FSR.
Calibrate peristaltic pump to desired speed (300 mL/min) diameter - 1 cm
Place one end of tubing in the water reservoir and one end in the bucket, ensuring that the reservoir is above the bucket. 
Run the program and allow for a few measurements to populate 
Start pumping water and stop when desired.

## Discrete
Steps:
Repeat steps 1-6 from continuous
Pour water into the bucket in increments, taking measurements each time and recording readings. 

## Data Collection Process
*Have Microsoft Data Streamer add-in for Excel
Go to Data Streamer tab in Excel
Connect arduino uno to arduino IDE
Verify and upload FSR code on arduino IDE
“Connect Device” on Excel spreadsheet
Press “Start Data” in Excel
Press “Record Data”
Start applying designated amount of pressure at second 15 until second 60
Press “Stop Recording” after second 60
Title csv. file
Move csv. file to Google Drive

